{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When he strove</b> — like: <i>when they strove against YHWH</i>." "<b>Aram-naharaim</b> — some say: from the root of destroyed cities, [reading] ערים נצים." "And the sense of <b>and Joab turned</b> — as a sign that David was weakened, and afterward Joab weakened Aram."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {1 "The phrase ערים נצים (cities of enemies?) is obscure; translated hyper-literally as it appears."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:19.809634442Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}